 The normal high for the date is 59\u00b0F, and the record is 81\u00b0F (1999). The low of <strong>28\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13.","t_rec":"Pueblo is setting record highs far faster than chance","p_rec":"If Pueblo's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Pueblo has set <strong>52 standing record lows</strong>, fewer than the 71 that chance alone would give, and <strong class=\"sig\">193 record highs</strong>, far more than the 71 that chance alone would give. The 2010s hold the most record highs of any decade (65). Pueblo's all-time high is 109\u00b0F, on July 13, 2003.","t_chg":"Pueblo's nights cooled over the long run but have warmed since 1986. Its days have warmed.","p_chg":"Across 137 complete years: Pueblo's average low has fallen <strong class='sig'>\u22120.10\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range \u22120.17 to \u22120.04), about \u22121.4\u00b0F since 1889. Pueblo's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.37\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.31 to +0.43), about +5.0\u00b0F since 1889. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.81\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.48 to +1.15) and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.65\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.31 to +0.98). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in none; 5 months fell. Highs rose in 10 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Pueblo's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.01 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 12.0 inches a year. The wettest year was 1957 (23.09 in); the driest, 2002 (3.94 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 16 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}